<title>RUSSIA: Russia Prosecutor to report on frozen Minfins soon.</title>
<headline>Russia Prosecutor to report on frozen Minfins soon.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Prosecutor General will announce a decision soon on the problem surrounding frozen MinFin bonds, a top Finance Ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We applied to the Prosecutor General's office to settle the problem,&quot; First Deputy Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin told Reuters. &quot;The Prosecutor General's vision of the problem is that the freeze must be lifted. I asked him to make a corresponding announcement, which we are expecting in the next few days.&quot;</p>
<p>Russian police froze $10.729 million nominal of the bearer MinFin bonds in May as part of a criminal investigation. Last year, the authorities froze about $74 million of bonds, most of which were later unfrozen.</p>
<p>The total nominal value of all outstanding MinFin bonds is $11 billion.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
